# el++ engine fixture 34 (src/test.slop: test-ksc-engine-matches-reference).
# Rule (8) from its inst premise: A ⊑ ∃r.Self gives self(x, r) in round 1,
# and B reaches x only in round 3, through A ⊑ C ⊑ B, after the self fact
# was processed. So ∃r.B ⊑ D must fire when inst(x, B) arrives, from that
# side. Expect: A ⊑ B, A ⊑ C, A ⊑ D; C ⊑ B.
# Inside el++ whole: the engine must answer every class as the literal Psc
# reference does (test-ksc-engine-matches-reference).

@prefix : <http://example.org/t#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
:r a owl:ObjectProperty .
:A a owl:Class . :B a owl:Class . :C a owl:Class . :D a owl:Class .
:A rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty :r ; owl:hasSelf true ] , :C .
:C rdfs:subClassOf :B .
[ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty :r ; owl:someValuesFrom :B ] rdfs:subClassOf :D .
